{"id":"chocolate-chip-cooky-308o","title":"Chocolate Chip Cookies","category":"dessert","lang":"en","source":"https://www.epicurious.com/video/watch/epicurious-101-the-best-chocolate-chip-cookies-youll-ever-make","ingredients":[{"qty":"385 g","name":"bread flour","n":1},{"qty":"3 g","name":"baking powder","n":1},{"qty":"3 g","name":"baking soda","n":1},{"qty":"4 g","name":"kosher salt","n":1},{"qty":"226 g","name":"cold butter","n":2},{"qty":"200 g","name":"light brown sugar","n":3},{"qty":"145 g","name":"granulated sugar","n":3},{"qty":"2","name":"eggs, cold","n":4},{"qty":"10 g","name":"pure vanilla extract","n":4},{"qty":"145 g","name":"bittersweet chocolate, hand chopped","n":5},{"qty":"140 g","name":"semisweet chocolate, hand chopped","n":5}],"steps":["Whisk (1) together until evenly distributed.","Mix (2) briefly to loosen, about 15 sec. Do not cream.","Add (3). Mix just until butter looks coated in sugar.","Add (4). Mix. It will look broken, that's fine.","Add (1) all at once. Mix slowly until just combined, a few flour streaks left.","Fold in (5). Keep specks of butter visible.","Portion 120 g per cookie (about 1/2 cup measure), shape by hand.","Freeze about 1 h.","Bake from frozen at 375°F for about 19 min, rotating halfway.","Smack tray lightly out of the oven. Rest 10 min on tray, then cool fully on a wire rack."],"notes":["Start with all ingredients cold; do not overmix, to keep butter pockets and a tender center.","Pull when edges are set and center is slightly soft and underbaked (matte edges, slightly glossy center), not liquid.","Chocolate chips work: hand chop about half for shards.","Freeze portioned dough individually and bake 1 or 2 at a time."],"createdAt":"2026-11-08T17:07:02.181Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-08T17:07:02.181Z"},
{"id":"kung-pao-chicken-ds7k","title":"Kung Pao chicken","category":"main","lang":"en","source":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RI0QA_TeE7s","ingredients":[{"qty":"300 g","name":"chicken breast, chunky pieces","n":1},{"qty":"⅛ tsp","name":"bicarbonate of soda","n":1},{"qty":"1 tsp","name":"cornflour","n":1},{"qty":"2 pinches","name":"salt","n":1},{"qty":"2 tbsp","name":"water","n":1},{"qty":"1½ tbsp","name":"Shaoxing rice wine","n":2},{"qty":"1 tbsp","name":"Chinkiang vinegar","n":2},{"qty":"½ tsp","name":"Sichuan pepper, ground","n":2},{"qty":"1½ tsp","name":"ginger, finely diced","n":2},{"qty":"2 cloves","name":"garlic, finely diced","n":2},{"qty":"1 pinch","name":"salt","n":2},{"qty":"1 tsp","name":"dark soy sauce","n":2},{"qty":"1¼ tbsp","name":"sugar","n":2},{"qty":"1 tbsp","name":"vegetable oil","n":3},{"qty":"3–4","name":"large dried chillies","n":3},{"qty":"50 g","name":"peanuts (raw, or roasted)","n":4},{"qty":"3 tbsp","name":"water","n":5},{"qty":"2","name":"spring onions, finely sliced","n":6},{"qty":"1 tsp","name":"sesame oil","n":6}],"steps":["Mix (1). Cover, fridge 30 min.","Mix (2) until sugar + salt dissolve. Keep by the stove.","Low heat: (3) ~30 s, until chillies plump and blacken a bit. Scoop chillies out, keep the oil.","Medium heat: (4) 45 s. Scoop out, keep the oil.","High heat: chicken from (1) in one layer. Sear to a caramel crust, then stir until coloured all over. Remove.","(2) + (5) into the wok. Add back chillies + (4). Simmer 1 min.","Chicken back in. Stir-fry 3–4 min until coated dark and glossy.","Stir through (6). Serve with steamed jasmine rice."],"notes":["Bicarbonate breaks down the chewy proteins: that's what keeps the breast tender.","Video vs written recipe: the video uses 1 tbsp cornflour, 2 tbsp ginger, 1 tbsp sugar, raw peanuts and no sesame oil. Quantities here follow the written list.","No Chinkiang → ½ tbsp balsamic + ½ tbsp water. No Shaoxing → dry sherry. Sichuan pepper is optional."],"createdAt":"2026-11-08T17:15:00.000Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-08T18:20:00.000Z"},
